# Valgrind suppressions for the valgrind job in native-checks.yaml. tools/
# is .Rbuildignore'd, so nothing here reaches the tarball.
#
# R's cairo bitmap device (grDevices png(type = "cairo")) leaks inside
# cairo/pixman when it draws a raster and when it opens: the blocks belong
# to the device, not to zusvg. test-render.R's "grid and graphics draw the
# raster" opens png() and draws a nativeRaster to check that grid and base
# graphics take zusvg's output, which is what provokes them. Matched on
# R's cairo frames, so a leak from zusvg's own code is still reported.
{
   R-cairo-device-raster
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:Cairo_Raster
}
{
   R-cairo-device-open
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:CairoInitGroups
}
{
   R-cairo-device-new-page
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:BM_NewPage
}
{
   R-cairo-device-in-cairo
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:in_Cairo
}

